{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yxnnmudsp3foweosnxxvzocu7vux47qp4t2caxsij265kj5zqp7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation required no fixes — it is byte-identical to the C for every input tested.**\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single 12-line translation unit exposing one function:\n`float ldexp_q2(float y, int exp_q2)` — a quarter-exponent scaler using a\n4-entry `static const float` table and a `do/while` loop.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (3 artifacts, all derived mechanically)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both `.so`s → C exports exactly `ldexp_q2`; Rust exports `ldexp_q2`. **Symbol diff empty.** Includes the C `-O0` disassembly and `.rodata` dump, since two implementation-defined details are only visible there. No C source was skipped (CMakeLists compiles one file). |\n| `ERRORS.md` | Grep found **zero** `RETURN_ERROR`/`return -1`/`return NULL`/`assert`/range check, and there are no pointer or enum parameters. So the table enumerates the **17 degenerate/boundary/UB conditions** the C actually hits, each with its measured expected bit pattern. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **27 rows** = pruned cross-product of the 5 axes the C branches on (clamp branch, `e & 3` residue, shift regime `(e>>2) & 31` incl. the mod-32 wrap, loop trip count, `y` float class). |\n\nCargo declares **no `[features]`** and the C has **zero preprocessor conditionals** → exactly 1 build combination, verified with `cargo check --no-default-features` (lib + tests).\n\n## Phases B/C/D — 47 differential tests, all passing\n\nTests `dlopen` **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and call the exported symbols — the Rust crate is never linked directly, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is exercised. **Both** the debug and release `cdylib` are loaded and compared in every assertion.\n\nIncludes exhaustive sweeps: all 8193 `exp_q2 ∈ [-4096,4096]` × 24 float classes, and all 2²³ mantissas across 21 (binade × `exp_q2`) combinations — ~500M FFI calls total.\n\n## Key C behaviours the Rust correctly replicates\n\n- **UB negative shift count**: `1 << 30 >> (e >> 2)` with `e < 0`. gcc emits `sar %cl`, which x86 masks to 5 bits — the Rust `& 31` reproduces this rather than \"fixing\" the UB. (Cross-checked: C at `-O2` is bit-identical to `-O0`.)\n- `e & 3` on negative `e` stays in `0..3` (no OOB).\n- No early return for `exp_q2 <= 0` — the `do/while` always scales.\n- `INT_MIN` (`exp_q2 -= e` must not overflow-trap) and `INT_MAX` (17.9M iterations, terminates).\n- sNaN quieting / qNaN payload+sign preservation, signed zeros, `inf*0 → 0xffc00000`.\n\n## Harness validated by mutation testing\n\nPassing tests are only meaningful if they *can* fail, so I injected 10 broken Rust `.so`s. 7 were **caught** (early return, clamped shift, `e/4` vs `e>>2`, swapped table entries, `& 15` mask, 1-ulp table perturbation). The 3 survivors were each **proven semantically equivalent** — notably the `f64`-intermediate mutant: the `f32`×`f32` product needs ≤48 bits so it is exact in `f64`, meaning there is no double rounding (confirmed over 250M cases).\n\n`c_src/` sources are unmodified (md5 + mtimes unchanged); only the prescribed `c_src/build/` output directory was added. Run everything with `./run_verification.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":112218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":668,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"897a6dae-c4d8-4dc4-9afa-b04752460c06","uuid":"d6e2dbba-3401-4c3f-acf3-5774b53171d6","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:24:49.417Z"}
